course: dictionary
lesson: 14465
title: Formal words: partake
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Partake is a formal word, found in old stories, church services and polite invitations. It has three main meanings: to eat or drink something that is offered to you, to take part in an activity, and, in church, to receive communion, the bread and wine.
explain: «Please partake of the cake, everyone.» The clue is the cake and the word please. The host is offering food, so partake means to have some of it.
explain: «Ten children partake in the relay race.» The clue is the race. Partake means to join in. In everyday speech you would say join in or have some instead.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simple word. If «join in» fits the sentence and makes sense, you have found the meaning of partake.
fact: Partake means to eat or drink something offered to you, or to take part in something.
fact: Partake of means to have some of food or drink. Partake in means to join in an activity.
fact: Partake is a formal word. People use join in or have some in everyday speech.
fact: Partook is the past tense of partake: «They partook of the soup.» Partaken and partaking are other forms.
fact: At communion, Christians partake of the bread and wine.
exercise: «The guests were invited to partake of the feast.» What does partake mean here? | Cook a meal for the others | Leave early without saying goodbye | Sleep under a tree | *Eat or drink something offered
exercise: In everyday speech, what could you say instead of «partake in the games»? | Watch from the bench | *Join in | Break the rules | Sit down quietly
exercise: Which word is the past tense of partake? | *partook | partakes | partaking | partake
test: «Many people partake of the bread at church.» What does partake mean here? | Forget the bread | Throw bread to the birds | Bake bread for the shop | *Receive communion, the bread and wine
test: Which everyday words could replace partake in «Ten children partake in the relay race»? | Hide and seek | Run away from the race | *Join in | Forget the rules
exam: «The invitation said, "Please partake of the cake."» What does partake mean? | Clean the kitchen | Throw the cake away | *Have some of the cake | Sing a song
